ay, and mixed feeding = other milks/formula and breast milk used on the same day.</p></fn><fn id="tfn10-ehp0116-001085"><label>*</label><p><italic>p</italic> &#x0003c; 0.05,</p></fn><fn id="tfn11-ehp0116-001085"><label>**</label><p><italic>p</italic> &#x0003c; 0.02,</p></fn><fn id="tfn12-ehp0116-001085"><label>#</label><p><italic>p</italic> &#x0003c; 0.005, significant differences for contrasts within variable, using Mann&#x02013;Whitney test.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="t5-ehp0116-001085" position="float"><label>Table 5</label><caption><p>Full and reduced linear regression models for developmental outcomes at ages 36 and 48 months.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><th colspan="5" align="center" rowspan="1">Full regression model<hr/></th><th colspan="5" align="center" rowspan="1">Reduced regression model<hr/></th></tr><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Measure</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Statistic</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Ate fish/seafood during pregnancy</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Lncord mercury</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Adjusted <italic>R</italic><sup>2</sup></th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Model <italic>p</italic>-value</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">No.</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Ate fish/seafood during pregnancy</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Ln-cord mercury</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Adjusted <italic>R</italic><sup>2</sup></th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Model <italic>p</italic>-value</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">No.</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">MDI 12</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>b</italic></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2.49</td><td 